65906:+{"name": "opus-modernize-pr438-20260914-05", "role": "modernize", "model": "claude-opus-5", "model_id": "claude-opus-5[1m]", "operator": "meta", "pr": 438, "branch": "issue-436-diagonal-zero-direction-mass", "issue": 436, "start": "2026-09-14T06:45:51Z", "end": "2026-09-14T07:12:00Z", "commit": "bbf81dc0", "merge_commit": "920b68c7", "base": "b48d60aded3a3bcf797646a86f4e0ad29b319988", "head": "bbf81dc0", "files": ["MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean", "MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/DiagonalZeroDirectionMass.lean", "blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex"], "changes": ["merge github/main into issue-436-diagonal-zero-direction-mass (150 commits behind; one import-list conflict in MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean resolved by keeping all of main's imports plus the branch's DiagonalZeroDirectionMass line)", "de-duplication: ZeroDirectionMass.lean auto-merged to main's byte-identical copy, leaving one copy of aLinePointDist_zero_direction_mass in the tree", "blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex: add subordinate node lem:line-point-zero-direction-mass after rem:ld-win-zero-direction with \\lean tags for both public declarations, statement- and proof-level \\leanok, and honest \\uses"], "changed_lines": 84, "status": "complete", "outcome": "updated", "lane_launched": true, "ci": "not run locally (delegated to the lane); lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Lines green (9157 jobs) on the head", "note": "Modernization pass for PR 438 (branch issue-436-diagonal-zero-direction-mass, issue 436) on today's main (github/main = b48d60aded3a3bcf797646a86f4e0ad29b319988, 'chore(telemetry): GitHub record snapshot'). Outcome UPDATED, not superseded. Supersede check: git diff --name-only github/main...HEAD listed three paths, MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean, MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/ZeroDirectionMass.lean and MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/DiagonalZeroDirectionMass.lean. Half of that IS already on main and half is not. ZeroDirectionMass.lean exists on github/main and its single public theorem MIPStarRE.QPBT.aLinePointDist_zero_direction_mass is byte-identical there (git show of both sides matches line for line, and main already consumes it at MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/NondegeneratePastingMass.lean:52), and main's Lines.lean already carries its re-export import. But the PR's actual deliverable, the theorem issue #436 scopes as 'prove only dLinePointDist_zero_direction_mass_le', is ABSENT from main: git grep for dLinePointDist_zero_direction over github/main returns nothing at all, and git cat-file -e github/main:.../DiagonalZeroDirectionMass.lean fails, so the module does not exist on main. The branch was 3 ahead / 150 behind. Merge: git merge --no-edit github/main produced exactly one conflict, an import-list conflict in MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean where main had added AffineEvaluation, FiberCollision and ZeroDirectionMass while the branch had added ZeroDirectionMass and DiagonalZeroDirectionMass. It was resolved by keeping every one of main's imports and adding only the branch's DiagonalZeroDirectionMass line, so the resolution is main's list plus one line; no import was dropped. ZeroDirectionMass.lean auto-merged to main's text, which de-duplicates the PR's copy without a deletion being needed: git diff github/main -- that path is now empty, so there is exactly one copy of aLinePointDist_zero_direction_mass in the tree, main's. No theorem, proof or hypothesis was dropped or weakened; the protected statement and proof of dLinePointDist_zero_direction_mass_le and its private helper dLineDescOf_ldDLineCL_direction are byte-identical to their pre-merge text. Merge commit 920b68c7; the repo's own merge-loss guard passed ('ok (base 13409f63dea1,5922ecc4d569, branch 480950ffd435, incoming b48d60aded3a)'). The stale-branch API worry did not materialise: prefixProjection_idempotent, Distribution.map_map, uniformDistribution_map_equiv, uniformDistribution_map_fst, avgOver_mono, Distribution.avgOver_map, chiIndex and