ype\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"prior_review\\\": {\\n    \\\"id\\\": 5122160565,\\n    \\\"commit_id\\\": \\\"af97ea9171beb99a47f2594495e37be353056a71\\\",\\n    \\\"state\\\": \\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\n    \\\"submitted_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T17:09:51Z\\\",\\n    \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- mipstarre-review pr=229 head=af97ea9171beb99a47f2594495e37be353056a71 -->\\\\n# Review \\\\u2014 PR 229 @ af97ea9171be\\\\n\\\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=APPROVED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\\\\n\\\\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-05T17:09:46Z \\\\u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\\\n\\\\nBranch `issue-135-low-degree-soundness-transport` onto `main`; merge base `a00e54060cdafec57c21460cfbe52d248242891a`; head `af97ea9171beb99a47f2594495e37be353056a71`.\\\\n\\\\n## Findings\\\\n\\\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\\\\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\\\\n\\\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\\\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:88` \\\\u2014 Replace \\\\u201cmature error\\\\u201d with \\\\u201cerror bound of the low individual degree theorem\\\\u201d; the current phrase describes formalization status rather than mathematics.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/SeedIndexedSoundness.lean:17` \\\\u2014 Replace \\\\u201cdilated/original/compressed carriers\\\\u201d in the module docstring with the corresponding Hilbert-space terminology.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\n\\\\n## Code review\\\\n\\\\n**APPROVED** for head `af97ea9171beb99a47f2594495e37be353056a71`. No unresolved blocker or requires-changes finding remains. The authoritative on-disk patch matches the checkout\\\\u2019s diff against the supplied merge base.\\\\n\\\\n### Mathematical review\\\\n\\\\nThe seed-indexed proof correctly distinguishes preservation of the two point/polynomial relations from recovery of polynomial/polynomial consistency. It does not assume that compressing both correlated registers preserves their joint correlations. Instead, it derives point agreement with error `9\\\\u03b5`, applies `consistencyDefect_trans_le` to obtain error `E + 2\\\\u221a(9\\\\u03b5 + E)`, and applies the polynomial collision estimate to add `md/q`. The subsequent absorption uses the established constants with `C\\\\u2080 = 10`; the directly indexed specialization uses `C\\\\u2080 = 1`.\\\\n\\\\nThe scalar absorption helper\\\\u2019s hypotheses are explicitly stated and discharged at both soundness applications. They are not additional assumptions on either soundness theorem.\\\\n\\\\n### Statement integrity audit\\\\n\\\\n- **Paper assumptions:** `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413`, `lem:ld-soundness`, quantifies universal constants before admissible parameters, positive error, and a projective strategy succeeding with probability at least `1\\\\u2212\\\\u03b5`.\\\\n- **Lean assumptions:** Both new soundness specializations preserve that quantifier structure and explicitly restrict the simultaneity parameter to `k = 1`. The seed-indexed theorem retains `LdParams`, including divisibility; the directly indexed theorem concerns the separately documented game without that requirement. Neither adds a proof-obligation input.\\\\n- **Paper conclusion:** Two uniformly point-averaged consistency relations and one global polynomial consistency relation, all bounded by the displayed `deltaLd` error.\\\\n- **Lean conclusion:** All three relations are preserved, with polynomial-tuple POVMs on the original strategy spaces.\\\\n- **Verdict:** Faithful, explicitly documented one-coordinate specialization and directly indexed auxiliary\\\\u2014not a claimed proof of the unrestricted theorem. The new blueprint nodes state these restrictions.\\\\n\\\\nI also checked the provider against `references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180`, `thm:main-formal`, and the cited NEEXP combining argument. The revised gap note correctly distinguishes the established direct proof from the still-unverified printed tensor-code route.\\\\n\\\\n### Prior findings\\\\n\\\\nAll attached findings are addressed:\\\\n- Original F1: the gap note\\\\u2019s earlier status sections now describe the completed one-coordinate transport.\\\\n- F2\\\\u2013F6: the error status, subordinate support nodes, dependencies, compression claim, and numerical constant are corrected.\\\\n- F7\\\\u2013F11: the cited docstring and terminology changes are present.\\\\n- The separately numbered triangle-inequality F1 is resolved: the proof now attributes chaining to the triangle inequality and polynomial recovery to the codeword estimate.\\\\n\\\\n### Validation and residual risk\\\\n\\\\nAll three substantive Lean files type-check: `SeedIndexedSoundness.lean`, `Transport/PointAgreement.lean`, and `Soundness.lean`. The only emitted warning is the existing, documented arbitrary-`k` `sorry`.\\\\n\\\\nAxiom inspection of both new soundness theorems and `ldPointPair_consistencyDefect_le` reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; no `sorryAx` occurs.\\\\n\\\\nGeneral-`k` soundness and the downstream dimension-extension application remain explicitly open. I did not rerun a full project or blueprint build. The external `lean-conventions` reference was unavailable locally; repository integrity instructions were used. No files or GitHub records were modified.\\\\n\\\\n## Prose review\\\\n\\\\n**Category A:** No unresolved mathematical-equivalence or status mismatch found in the changed entries. The two soundness specializations explicitly impose \\\\\\\\(k=1\\\\\\\\), retain universally quantified constants, and state the three required consistency conclusions. The directly indexed domain correctly omits divisibility, while the seed-indexed domain retains it. The scalar absorption lemma displays its hypotheses separately rather than adding them to the paper theorem.\\\\n\\\\nThe new blueprint entries cover the public auxiliary results. The triangle-inequality dependency and its role in recovering evaluated-polynomial consistency are now explicit. The numerical witnesses agree with `exists_directLdTransportConstants`: \\\\\\\\(a=2.5\\\\\\\\cdot10^{10}\\\\\\\\) for the seed-indexed argument and \\\\\\\\(a=2.5\\\\\\\\cdot10^9\\\\\\\\) for the direct argument, with \\\\\\\\(b=1/80000\\\\\\\\).\\\\n\\\\n**Category B:** Two terminology corrections remain under `docs/mathematical_language.md`:\\\\n- **F1:** \\\\u201cMature error\\\\u201d occurs in the section heading and prose at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:88`, `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:91`, and `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:203`. Use \\\\u201cerror bound of the low individual degree theorem,\\\\u201d or simply \\\\u201cresulting error bound\\\\u201d where the theorem has already been identified. No identifier changes are needed.\\\\n- **F2:** The Hilbert-space correction made in the blueprint should also be applied to the new module docstring. At `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/SeedIndexedSoundness.lean:17`, use \\\\u201cextended Hilbert spaces\\\\u201d; at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/SeedIndexedSoundness.lean:18` and `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/SeedIndexedSoundness.lean:27`, use \\\\u201coriginal Hilbert spaces.\\\\u201d These terms identify the mathematical spaces and avoid the misleading suggestion that compression creates separate \\\\u201ccompressed carriers.\\\\u201d\\\\n\\\\n**Prior-ledger triage:** The original F1\\\\u2013F11 and the separately numbered triangle-inequality F1 are addressed at their cited locations: status sections are updated, auxiliary blueprint entries are present, dependencies and constants are corrected, the compression obstruction is no longer overstated, and the cited interface, heartbeat, packet, and blueprint-carrier wording is removed. The two findings above concern remaining wording in the new Lean documentation.\\\\n\\\\n**Summary:** 0 equivalence mismatches, 0 newly identified invalid status tags, 2 prose issues. This was a read-only source review; builds were not rerun. Arbitrary-\\\\\\\\(k\\\\\\\\) soundness and the downstream dimension-\\\\\\\\(2m+2\\\\\\\\) application remain explicitly documented limitations, not new findings.\\\\n\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"fixed_review\\\": {\\n    \\\"id\\\": 5122284090,\\n    \\\"commit_id\\\": \\\"6e754fc61c33e4013f7a8c246fa807c55eb48091\\\",\\n    \\\"state\\\": \\\"COMMENTED\\\",\\n    \\\"submitted_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T17:42:07Z\\\",\\n    \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- mipstarre-review pr=229 head=6e754fc61c33e4013f7a8c246fa807c55eb48091 -->\\\\n# Review \\\\u2014 PR 229 @ 6e754fc61c33\\\\n\\\\nVERDICT: APPROVED (code=APPROVED, prose=APPROVED)\\\\n\\\\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-05T17:42:03Z \\\\u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\\\n\\\\nBranch `issue-135-low-degree-soundness-transport` onto `main`; merge base `a00e54060cdafec57c21460cfbe52d248242891a`; head `6e754fc61c33e4013f7a8c246fa807c55eb48091`.\\\\n\\\\n## Findings\\\\n\\\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\\\\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\\\\n\\\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\\\n<!-- no findings -->\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\n\\\\n## Code review\\\\n\\\\nReviewed head `6e754fc61c33e4013f7a8c246fa807c55eb48091`. The authoritative on-disk patch matches the checkout\\\\u2019s diff against the supplied merge base. I found no remaining blocker or requires-changes issue.\\\\n\\\\n### Statement Integrity\\\\n\\\\nThe source `lem:ld-soundness` in `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413` quantifies universal constants before parameters and strategies, assumes projectivity and success at least \\\\\\\\(1-\\\\\\\\varepsilon\\\\\\\\), and concludes three polynomial-measurement consistency bounds.\\\\n\\\\n`exists_ld_soundness_of_k_eq_one` preserves these quantifiers, hypotheses, error-function shape, and conclusions, with the explicit restriction \\\\\\\\(k=1\\\\\\\\). The blueprint records that restriction in a separate formalization-support theorem at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:291`; it does not present this as the unrestricted source theorem. The directly indexed specialization is likewise identified as an auxiliary result for a different game.\\\\n\\\\n**Verdict:** faithful specialization with the documented parameter-domain encoding; no additional proof-debt hypothesis. The absorption helper\\\\u2019s numerical hypotheses are explicit in its auxiliary blueprint statement and are discharged internally in both soundness proofs.\\\\n\\\\n### Mathematical Review\\\\n\\\\nThe seed-indexed proof correctly avoids assuming that compression preserves global polynomial consistency. It transports the two point/polynomial relations exactly, uses the point-agreement branch to obtain \\\\\\\\(9\\\\\\\\varepsilon\\\\\\\\), and applies `consistencyDefect_trans_le` with the correct orientation. The collision estimate then yields\\\\n\\\\\\\\[\\\\nE+2\\\\\\\\sqrt{9\\\\\\\\varepsilon+E}+md/q.\\\\n\\\\\\\\]\\\\nFor \\\\\\\\(T=E+md/q+\\\\\\\\varepsilon\\\\\\\\le1\\\\\\\\), the proof bounds this by \\\\\\\\(10\\\\\\\\sqrt T\\\\\\\\). The selected constants agree with `exists_directLdTransportConstants`: \\\\\\\\(a=2.5\\\\\\\\cdot10^{10}\\\\\\\\), \\\\\\\\(b=1/80000\\\\\\\\) for seed-indexed soundness, and \\\\\\\\(a=2.5\\\\\\\\cdot10^9\\\\\\\\) for direct soundness.\\\\n\\\\nThe underlying LDT statement at `references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180` and the corrected Lean `mainFormal` require sampling bounds that the chosen parameter \\\\\\\\(2560000m^3d\\\\\\\\) satisfies internally. No such obligation leaks into the new public soundness statements.\\\\n\\\\n### Prior Findings\\\\n\\\\nAll attached findings are addressed:\\\\n\\\\n- Initial **F1**: the divisibility note now distinguishes established transport from the open general-\\\\\\\\(k\\\\\\\\) and downstream work, including `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex:35`.\\\\n- Initial **F2\\\\u2013F4**: the error-status remark, auxiliary declaration coverage, and proof dependencies are updated at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:285`, `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:311`, and `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:300`.\\\\n- Initial **F5\\\\u2013F6**: the compression claim is qualified and the constant corrected at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:305` and `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:308`.\\\\n- Initial **F7**: direct correspondence and parameter bounds are identified as established at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:42`.\\\\n- Initial **F8\\\\u2013F11**: the cited carrier/interface terminology, heartbeat rationale, and \\\\u201cseparate packet\\\\u201d wording have been replaced or removed in the changed passages.\\\\n- Later **F1** concerning triangle attribution: explicitly corrected at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:306`, with the dependency included.\\\\n- Final **F1\\\\u2013F2**: the remaining \\\\u201cmature error\\\\u201d and carrier terminology are corrected at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/Soundness.lean:88` and `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/SeedIndexedSoundness.lean:17`.\\\\n\\\\n### Validation And Residual Risk\\\\n\\\\nStatic inspec
